{
  "_rules": {
    "start": "Comfort starts at 1. Outside shelter it stays 1: no piece counts unless the player is in shelter (Player.InShelter).",
    "shelter": "+1 while in shelter.",
    "radius": "Pieces count within 10 m of the player, measured from the player's position to the piece's pivot (transform.position), not its bounds; ghost (placement preview) pieces never count.",
    "groups": "Within each comfort group (Fire, Bed, Banner, Chair, Table, Carpet, Display, Decor, Garland, Lantern, Leisure) only the highest-comfort piece counts.",
    "group_none": "Group None pieces each count, but only once per distinct name token (m_name), so two of the same piece add once.",
    "lit": "A piece with m_comfortObject (needs_lit) counts only while that child object is active, else it counts 0 and a lit lower piece of the same group counts instead. Fire pits and the ceiling/standing brazier use '_enabled_high': on only while burning and dry (it goes off while raining without a roof over the fire, or in wind >= 0.8 with under 70% cover). The hearth uses '_enabled': burning is enough, rain does not matter. The hot tub ('_Enabled', run as a smelter) counts while it has wood fuel and its smoke is not blocked.",
    "always_on": "Pieces without m_comfortObject count whether lit or not (bonfire, blue-flame standing brazier, lanterns).",
    "rested": "Rested lasts 8 min + 1 min per comfort level above 1 (SE_Rested: m_baseTTL + (comfort - 1) * 60 s).",
    "seasonal": "seasonal=true pieces (Piece.m_enabled false) are buildable only while their season is active.",
    "tool": "Piece table that offers the piece (Hammer, Feaster for placed meads); null means not player-buildable (trader camp fires, female/male armour stands, an old bench copy).",
    "source": "Read offline from the game's prefab bundle (SoftRef c4210710, ZNetScene prefabs) on 2026-10-05; English names from the game's localization CSV."
